    "id": "f3_h3_dsp8_nodal_smooth_high_tail_domination",
    "title": "DSP8 nodal/smooth high-tail domination",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On every retained product fiber, the nodal signed-disjoint distance-six graph has maximum degree three while the total disjoint graph has the proved multiplicity lower bound. Hence nodal edges are dominated targetwise by smooth edges for antipodal-free P>=33 and antipodal P>=35. The high-tail quotient-weighted moment is at most twice its smooth part; the bounded lower multiplicity bands and the smooth moment remain open.",
